// specs/0077 — SIBERIA'S FOREST MASKS, AS DATA. GENERATED, never hand-edited:
//
//   node tools/regions/siberia-mask-grids.mjs --sib <a built --legacy siberia tree>
//
// 0052 W4 built the region's forest from the bundle's canopy/cliff/slope grids
// and SUBSTITUTED a distance-to-centreline for siberia's stamped piste cut,
// then dropped its `bowl` and `glade` masks because nothing in the bundle
// carried them. Measured (renders/0077/GATE-0077.md): 1.340x the standalone's
// forest over the same ground, x2.86 in Siberia Bowl, x13.1 on the groomed
// pistes. D-23 says a streamed forest REPRODUCES the shipped one; this file is
// the missing input, read out of the standalone's own `masksAt` and encoded
// exactly like sib-canopy-data.mjs — u8, value/255, { span, n, ox, oy, b64 }.
//
//   CUT    clamp(groom*1.2 + pack*1.25 + cat*1.2 + lift*1.15 + chute*1.6
//                + wall*1.6, 0, 1) — the six channels siberia's forestDensity
//          reads ONLY through their weighted sum, so one grid carries them
//          exactly (bilinear is linear; the sum is linear) at a sixth of six
//          grids' heap.
//          The clamp saturates on 36186 of 262144 cells (max raw 4.00), all of them
//          deep inside a corridor where the density is zero at 0.26 either way;
//          the 0.26 CROSSING, which is the only thing the field can spend, lies
//          in the unsaturated tail and is carried exactly.
//   BOWL   the open alpine bowl (`MO`), raw — it enters through its own lerp.
//          55724 cells above the 0.08 threshold.
//   GLADE  the glade mask (`ML`), raw. 55 cells above 0.08.
//   GROOM  the groomed-piste mask (`MG`) and the packed base-area mask
//   PACK   (`MK`), raw — the rock loops test these on their own thresholds
//          (`groom > 0.35 || pack > 0.2` vetoes a boulder, `groom > 0.2`
//          vetoes a talus block) and not through the cut sum. 24972 boulder-veto
//          cells, 25930 talus-veto cells.
//   SLOPE6 `slopeAt(x, y, 6)` / 90 — the slope of the STAMPED surface, which is
//          what forest.mjs reads and what the cliff bundle's raw-3DEP SLOPE
//          grid is not. Max 77.1 deg. On its OWN lattice at n = 256
//          (6.50 m/px): it is terrain and not a corridor stamp, so it
//          costs more brotli than the other five together, and slopeAt() has
//          already smoothed it over a 6 m radius.
//
// 3.250 m/px over 1664 m centred on siberia's CORE, which covers the frame's
// forest box (CORE + 40 m) with the standalone raster's own 70 m of margin.
//
// RUN_LINES / STATIONS / BUILDINGS are the three GEOMETRIES siberia's own
// forest.mjs reads that the bundle's OSM tables are not: the 24 authored run
// centrelines its `distToRuns` walks (769 vertices), its 4 lift terminals
// (the bundle's OSM query answers sixteen, and a 34 m clear around twelve
// terminals siberia does not have is twelve holes in the forest), and the 4
// building footprints `forestDensity` refuses to plant inside.
export const CUT = { span: 1664.0, n: 512, ox: 105.00, oy: 35.00, b64: "" };
